# Settings for the network variant (./build.sh network). Copy to netboot.conf
# (not tracked by git) and set the URL of your distribution server(s). Sourced
# as bash.
#
# NETROOT_URL: base URL under which the distribution servers serve the network
# releases: <SERVER_URL>/network/ (server/server.conf.example). build.sh appends the image version, so the UKI it signs
# always loads the root image of exactly that build:
#   NETROOT_URL=http://arch.boot.internal/safespace/network/
#   -> safespace.netroot=http://arch.boot.internal/safespace/network/20261016-1830/
#      and the initrd fetches .../20261016-1830/root.img and root.verity
#
# An IP address needs no DNS at all. A host name works too: the initrd resolves
# it with the DNS servers from its DHCP lease (see NETBOOT.md, "A host name
# instead of an IP address").
# Several URLs (space separated) are tried in order: a name with an address as
# fallback, or several distribution servers:
#   NETROOT_URL="http://arch.boot.internal/safespace/network/ http://10.0.0.2/safespace/network/"
# The URLs are part of the signed kernel command line; changing them means
# rebuilding the image.
NETROOT_URL=http://arch.boot.internal/safespace/network/
